<!--
  ============================================================================
  BehemothArtUpres_StarWarsAnimalCollection.xml   Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-29
  ============================================================================
  Item: BEHEMOTH_ART_UPRES_1

  Owner, verbatim, mid-AFK: "improve the art of the Behemoth that did not come
  from the Craigs. (it looks like a dinosaur with something coming out of its
  jaw). It's very low res and should be made as large as the Behemoth that DID
  come from the Craigs."

  Two "Behemoth" creatures exist in the live mod set - AA_Behemoth (Alpha
  Animals, a dragon, already 512x512) is NOT this. The target is `Behemoth`
  (PawnKindDef, Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued) -
  mlie.starwarsanimalcollection): an "armoured shaggy quadruped" with a
  triceratops-like frilled head and two curved tusks - exactly "a dinosaur
  with something coming out of its jaw" - shipped at 256x256. Redrawn here at
  512x512 (2x pixel resolution, matching AA_Behemoth's canvas), SAME
  silhouette and design - this is a resolution/quality upgrade, not a
  redesign. drawSize is untouched (art-only item).

  Confirmed via the live def dump and the mod's own XML
  (.../3497316713/1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Races_Animal_SW.xml:3664):
  PawnKindDef[defName="Behemoth"]/lifeStages has THREE <li> (calf/juvenile/
  adult) that all reuse the SAME four texPath stems at different drawSize -
  one PatchOperationReplace per stem, matched by the node's CURRENT VALUE
  (not by li[N] position - GrimTerraTexPaths_Fix.xml's own reasoning: a
  positional index breaks the moment anything reorders the list), covers all
  three life stages in a single op.

  🔑 north is IDENTICAL between sexes. Verified: behemoth_m_north.png and
  behemoth_f_north.png are byte-for-byte identical in the donor's own art (a
  rear/back-of-head view has no tusks or face to differ). So ONE redrawn
  north image is deployed twice, under both the male and female texPath
  stems, rather than drawn separately - guarantees they stay identical rather
  than merely similar.

  🪤 texPath is NOT namespaced by mod - ContentFinder resolves a relative
  texPath against every active mod's Textures folder. Reusing the donor's own
  string (swanimals/Behemoth/Behemoth_m) verbatim would create a same-path
  collision with the donor's own bundled art (both mods then offer a resource
  at that path; which one wins depends on load order, not on this patch).
  New art therefore ships under a DISTINCT relative path -
  swanimals/Behemoth/JawaBehemoth_* - never the donor's own stem.

  dessicatedBodyGraphicData/femaleDessicatedBodyGraphicData ship ONE image
  each, no facing suffix - matching the donor's own convention (there is no
  behemoth_m_dessicated_south.png, just behemoth_m_dessicated.png).
  Graphic_Multi's bare-path fallback (ContentFinder.Get on the un-suffixed
  path, before it errors) is what makes a single corpse image satisfy every
  rotation; this patch mirrors that rather than fighting it.

  Verified against the live def dump before writing this file
  (2026-08-29T20-07-29Z capture) and against validate_patch.py.

  ⛔ DO NOT EDIT THE WORKSHOP FOLDER. Steam overwrites it on the next update.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Behemoth"]/lifeStages/li/bodyGraphicData[texPath="swanimals/Behemoth/Behemoth_m"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>swanimals/Behemoth/JawaBehemoth_m</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Behemoth"]/lifeStages/li/femaleGraphicData[texPath="swanimals/Behemoth/Behemoth_f"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>swanimals/Behemoth/JawaBehemoth_f</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Behemoth"]/lifeStages/li/dessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="swanimals/Behemoth/Behemoth_m_Dessicated"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>swanimals/Behemoth/JawaBehemoth_m_Dessicated</texPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Behemoth"]/lifeStages/li/femaleDessicatedBodyGraphicData[texPath="swanimals/Behemoth/Behemoth_f_Dessicated"]/texPath</xpath>
          <value><texPath>swanimals/Behemoth/JawaBehemoth_f_Dessicated</texPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
